AB  - Communication is critical in today's world, especially in education, academics have been interested in the methods used to communicate knowledge to students and the educational processes are both heading toward digitalization. The study aims to provide innovative learning method that makes pre-school children's learning more interactive. The system integrated an object recognition-based learning instructional robot thereby making learning Alphabets and numbers more interesting with projected Text-to-Speech (TTS) to attract children's attention. In this work, we present preprocessing of images and classification algorithms which are pretrained with a standard dataset intended for Letters and numbers. Tensor flow was used to train, test, and validate the Convolution Neural network (CNN) model against the pretrain real-world image data. Optical Character Recognition (OCR) converts the detected object into text and fed to the Text-to-Speech algorithm which vocals out the name of the recognized object. Experimental Design Science Research (E-DSR) approach was employed in this study which consists of six steps viz: Identifying the problem, Defining Objectives, Designing and developing, Demonstrating and Evaluating the artifact, and communicating the results. A phone camera attached on an Arduino microcontroller that has few sensors incorporated in it serves as the prototype's eye for the obstacle avoidance robot system. The findings demonstrated that a robot could navigate a classroom while avoiding obstacles, and that it was possible to develop application that could categorize images based on a set of objects it was trained on. An experiment was carried out to gauge the system's efficacy. The finding that children were interacting with a robot and imitating the sound made by TTS led to the conclusion that an interactive system could increase preschoolers' learning effectiveness.
