AB  - Without a doubt, Food is a vital part of any Human's life, not only because of the nutrients provided but also the excellent taste. Subsequently, countless great people have invested their life in exchange for this enjoyment upon Human taste buds. However, even a three-Michelin-starred chef cannot remember the detailed steps to all the dishes, and ordinary citizens do not have the time or energy to create their recipes. This paper proposes an aid system that uses neural networks to achieve accurate recipe projections to facilitate life. A deep learning system based on Decoder and Encoder is implemented using CNN and Transformer. The CNN reduces the memory cost by transforming the image to a vector, achieving faster processing. The Transformer is used to determine ingredients' presence and combine the information of existing dishes to construct an instruction. Such a network can facilitate food production and research. It is making the creation of unique dishes convenient by revolutionizing the method of recording. After the model is created, the backbone network of CNN layers are manipulated to test for the best result. Backbone network tests include ResNet50, ResNet152 without attention, ResNet152 with attention, Vgg16, and AlexNet. Out of all tested, ResNet152 is resulted with the highest iou (Intersection over Union), and without-attention is chosen as it possesses less complexity than its counterpart. Then, knowledge distillation is applied to decrease the complexity and size of the model. This process used the complex model as a trainer to the student model by basing the student training on the result of the teacher model, achieving a similar level of accuracy with a significantly lower complexity and size. This decrease in complexity increases the portable capability of the model, potentially applying into applications and websites on devices in the future without consuming much memory.
ER  - 

